---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = new Date("2026-11-21");
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Tal Israeli"
  description="The terms that apply when you visit and use Tal Israeli's personal website, talisrae.li."
>
  <fieldset>
    <legend>Terms of Service</legend>
    <p class="updated">
      Last updated:{" "}
      <time datetime={lastUpdated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>
        {lastUpdated.toLocaleDateString("en-US", { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric", timeZone: "UTC" })}
      </time>
    </p>

    <p>
      Welcome to <strong>talisrae.li</strong> (the &ldquo;Website&rdquo;), the personal website of Tal Israeli
      (&ldquo;I&rdquo;, &ldquo;me&rdquo; or &ldquo;my&rdquo;). By visiting or using the Website, you agree to these
      Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please do not use the Website.
    </p>

    <h2>1. About the Website</h2>
    <p>
      The Website is a personal portfolio. It presents information about me, my education and my projects, and ways to
      get in touch with me. It does not offer any products or paid services, and you do not need an account to use it.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>You agree to use the Website only for lawful purposes. In particular, you agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Website or the systems that host it;</li>
      <li>interfere with or disrupt the Website, for example by overloading it with automated requests;</li>
      <li>use the Website or its content to mislead others, or to impersonate me or anyone else.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p>
      Unless stated otherwise, the content of the Website, including its text, images, design and logos, is owned by me
      or used with permission, and is protected by copyright and other laws. You may view and share links to the
      Website, and quote short excerpts with attribution, for personal and non-commercial purposes. Any other use
      requires my prior written permission.
    </p>
    <p>
      Logos and trademarks of third parties, such as academic institutions, belong to their respective owners and are
      shown only to identify them. The Website's source code is publicly visible on GitHub; that visibility does not by
      itself grant a license to reuse it, except as stated in the repository.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>
      The Website links to third-party websites and services, such as LinkedIn, GitHub, X and the sharing options in the
      &ldquo;Share&rdquo; menu. I do not control those websites and am not responsible for their content, policies or
      practices. Your use of them is governed by their own terms.
    </p>

    <h2>5. No Warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The Website and its content are provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo;, for general
      information only. I try to keep everything accurate and up to date, but I make no warranties of any kind, express
      or implied, about the Website's accuracy, completeness or availability. Nothing on the Website is professional
      advice.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, I will not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental or consequential
      damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, the Website or any content or third-party website linked
      from it.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      With your permission only, the Website uses Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to understand how visitors use
      it. How your information is handled, and how to change your choice, is explained in the{" "}
      <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to These Terms</h2>
    <p>
      I may update these Terms from time to time. The updated version will be posted on this page with a new &ldquo;Last
      updated&rdquo; date. Your continued use of the Website after a change means you accept the updated Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Governing Law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Israel. Any dispute arising from them or from your use of the
      Website will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts in Haifa, Israel.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about these Terms, please email me at{" "}
      <a href="mailto:contact@talisrae.li">contact@talisrae.li</a>.
    </p>
  </fieldset>
</Layout>

<style lang="scss">
  .updated {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.25rem;
  }

  ul {
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  fieldset p {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
  }
</style>
